From 808c179b07a127fa50118f95c3d2eab8767427e7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucaci32u4 <lucaci32u4@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 08:50:27 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 4/4] Accept any one role's scope for tables shared by several
 rulesets

map_scope(roles=...) returned a single alternative holding every role's
scope, so an OAuth2 token needed the scopes of all rulesets a table belongs
to (part_part: part AND build; company_company: purchase, sales AND return
order). The role check for the same request
(users.permissions.check_user_permission) accepts any one of the roles, so a
token issued with exactly the scopes a role grants could not use that
role's tables.

Return one alternative per role instead, which TokenMatchesOASRequirements
treats as OR.

map_scope(roles=...) has three callers, all affected:
- InvenTreeRoleScopeMixin (every endpoint of a multi-role table);
- DataImporterPermission (the data importer endpoints: writes needed the
  r:change scope of all eleven roles, now any one of them; reads keep
  g:read);
- ContentTypePermission (GenericMetadataView, the generic metadata
  endpoints: every method needed the scope of all eleven roles, now any
  one of them).
The object-level checks of the last two are unchanged.

The OpenAPI security requirements of these endpoints change (one
requirement per role), so bump the API version to 557.

Add unit tests for map_scope, the scope check on a multi-role table
(PartList), ContentTypePermission and DataImporterPermission.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
